    DAT_L3_html: '<code>api_keys.json</code> — the key from the <a href="keys.html">artwork service</a>, if you added one.',
    DAT_LEDE: 'Your library is stored on your own computer, in a single folder, as a plain text file. Nothing is uploaded and there is no account to register.',
    DAT_LNX: 'Linux',
    DAT_MOVE_H: 'Moving to another machine',
    DAT_MOVE_P: 'Copy the folder across and Parallax finds it. Your games\' locations will not match, though — a different machine keeps its games somewhere else, and possibly on a different drive letter. Refresh the library once and every Steam game corrects itself; the ones you added by hand need pointing at again.',
    DAT_NET_H: 'What leaves your machine',
    DAT_NET_P: 'Three places, and each of them only when you ask: Steam, for the list of games you own and the hours you have played; SteamGridDB, for artwork; GitHub, to see whether there is a newer version. That is the entire list. Your library is never sent anywhere, there is no analytics of any kind in the app, and there is no account to sign in to.',
