    FOOT_SOURCE: 'Source',
    FR_1_H: 'Make an account',
    FR_1_P: 'This is a name for the library, kept on this machine. It is not an account with any service: nothing is sent anywhere, and there is no password unless you set one. Two people sharing a computer can keep separate libraries.',
    FR_2_H: 'Bring in your Steam games',
    FR_2_P2: 'Cover art and banners are fetched at the same time. A large library takes a few minutes; you can use the app while it works.',
    FR_2_P_html: 'Paste your Steam profile link, or just your Steam name, and Parallax fetches everything you own. It needs your profile to be public — Steam hides game lists by default, and a private one comes back empty rather than with an error worth reading.',
    FR_3_H: 'Add what Steam does not know about',
    FR_3_P: 'Games from Epic, GOG, the Xbox app, an emulator, or something you compiled yourself. Type the name and Parallax looks for it on your disk — Steam\'s own records first, then the folders games are usually kept in, on every drive.',
    FR_3_P2: 'If it finds it, the location is filled in for you. If it does not, it asks you to point at the file rather than guessing.',
    FR_4_H: 'Arrange the shelf',
    FR_4_P2: 'Filters narrow it to what is installed, or to one platform. The setting sticks, so the shelf looks the way you left it.',
    FR_4_P_html: 'Sort by name, by hours played, or by the dominant colour of the cover art. The last is useful in a large library, where a game is often easier to recognise by sight than by title.',
    FR_H1: 'The first ten minutes.',
    FR_KICKER: 'First run',
    FR_LEDE: 'What to do when you open Parallax for the first time: create an account, import your library, add games and arrange them.',
    FR_NEXT_html: 'Something not behaving? <a href="trouble.html">The troubleshooting guide</a> covers what goes wrong most often.',
    FR_PLAY_H: 'Then press Play',
    FR_PLAY_P: 'A Steam game is started through Steam, which handles Proton, cloud saves and the overlay. Anything else Parallax runs itself, on Linux through Proton or Wine when the game is a Windows one. Hours are counted either way, and a game you have not installed offers to find or fetch it rather than doing nothing.',
    FR_PROPS_P_html: 'Every game has a <strong>Properties</strong> panel for the settings that decide how it starts: the Proton build, launch options and environment variables. Left alone, it chooses sensible defaults, and most games never need anything else.',
    IDX_ASK_html: 'Something not covered here? <a href="https://github.com/ArdaYalinOzkan/parallax-launcher/issues">Open an issue</a> — it is read.',
